    "verdict": "implicit ALS (0.285) dominates; popularity (0.137) beats every memory-based engine and explicit MF (0.047); item-based CF collapses (0.002). This is the well-documented Cremonesi/Koren/Turrin 2010 finding: under plain leave-one-out, a non-personalized popularity baseline matches sophisticated algorithms, RMSE does not imply top-N accuracy, and correlation-based item-kNN performs extremely poorly. Standard fix: exclude top-popular head items from the LOO test set."
  },
