  "overall_verdict": "The system's from-scratch engines are within the published default-parameter range on ml-100k rating prediction (RMSE 0.987-1.009 vs published 0.93-0.98 for the k-NN family), closing most of the gap that tuned/external implementations get. Its implicit ALS is the strongest LOO ranker. The agentic layer does not help raw ranking on this data but provides the one thing pure CF cannot: explicit constraint compliance (1.0 genre precision vs 0.04). For honest LOO numbers, future runs should exclude the top-2% popular head items."
